            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of the unilateral activation of brain hemispheres on visceral pain sensitivity in BALB/c mice].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1374-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A hemispheric asymmetry of the visceral pain sensitivity control was revealed in the BALB/c mice: animals with the left hemisphere inactivation did not differ from sham-operated control mice in respect to the pain response parameters. A right hemisphere inactivation reduced or suppressed the pain response. This suggests that the right hemisphere domineers in the visceral pain control.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
